WEBVTT

00:08:27.716 --> 00:08:31.076
and are able to see just
how complete this ichthyosaur is.

00:08:31.116 --> 00:08:33.556
So you start from the very
tip of the snout

00:08:33.596 --> 00:08:36.556
all the way down
to the penny-sized vertebrae.

00:08:36.556 --> 00:08:37.756
Pretty cool.

00:08:37.756 --> 00:08:40.916
And we're even able
to pick out individual bones

00:08:40.956 --> 00:08:43.356
and look at them in three
dimensions like this.

00:08:43.396 --> 00:08:44.836
This is the sort of techniques

00:08:44.876 --> 00:08:47.076
that are sort of
revolutionizing paleontology.

00:08:47.116 --> 00:08:51.036
We're able to capture all of this data
whilst the ichthyosaur sat in the ground.

00:08:51.076 --> 00:08:52.916
So before we've even removed anything.

00:08:52.916 --> 00:08:54.836
Now we've taken that out of the ground,

00:08:54.836 --> 00:08:55.996
we still have this data,

00:08:56.036 --> 00:08:58.916
and we can send that to our colleagues
all around the world.